//// 01-compiler/01-checker row "`@block` tail form refused" (decision 2) — an
//// `@block` used as a value takes what its `return`s carry, never its tail
//// expression: `val a = @block { 1 + 2 };` has no valued `return` and is
//// `block-tail-value` at the block. The parent binary typed the block by its
//// tail and printed `3` on erlang, beam and wasm, `null` on commonJS.

pub fn main() {
    val a = @block { 1 + 2 };
    @print(a);
}
